        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Revert persistent shell and colors",
        "summary": "Reverts persistent PTY shell implementation, restoring child_process spawn for terminal commands. Removes node-pty dependency and associated terminal emulation logic. Updates handleRunTerminalCommand to return separate stdout and stderr streams instead of combined PTY output. Affects npm-app CLI, tool handlers, and backend prompt processing.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T17:37:55.910Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The tool that runs shell commands in the assistant's coding workflow has switched how it captures command output. Instead of merging the normal output and the error output into one combined stream, it now returns them as two separate streams, so you can tell which messages were errors versus regular output. This also means the special terminal emulation software has been removed entirely, and the older, simpler method for launching commands is back in use. A couple of leftover pieces that only existed to support that older setup were cleaned up or stopped being tracked, but the way commands are run and their results shown is otherwise unchanged.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "dd3882e7d69b",
        "at": "2026-09-17T21:20:40.664Z"
