        "v": 5,
        "title": "Docs layout flexbox fix",
        "summary": "Docs layout uses flexbox for main content and mobile sheet. Sidebar links handle external subsections correctly. Updates `web/src/app/docs/layout.tsx` and `web/src/components/docs/doc-sidebar.tsx`. External subsection links now use `target=_blank`.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T17:37:42.370Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you open the documentation help pages on a phone or narrow screen, the main text and the side menu now line up more evenly instead of looking lopsided. On phones, the side menu that slides up from the bottom now takes up half the screen instead of a cramped third, and it has more room at the top so the text doesn't get hidden. Links that point to external subsections (like separate chapters on another page) now open in a new tab instead of swapping out what you're reading, so you won't lose your place while browsing. These are live today for anyone using the docs site.",
