      "eli5": {
        "text": "You are now seeing a small set of navigation links at the bottom of each documentation category page: when you finish reading one doc page, you\\u2019ll see a previous and next button based on the order of the documentation sections, so you can click through to the adjacent doc instead of hunting back to the sidebar. The links appear only on pages that belong to the docs section and only when a prior or following section exists; the very first page won\\u2019t show a previous link, and the last page won\\u2019t show a next link. The change is in place now, so anyone viewing the docs site will see the new prev/next navigation at the bottom of each doc page.",
